From: Abzu <abzu@localhost>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] gui: authorize privileged operations via doas(1)

Abzu overlay (see ../README.md): security pillar -- privileged GNUstep
operations must be authorized through doas(1), which honours /etc/doas.conf
(shipped by build/derivations/rootfs.nix under the Abzu policy) and fails
closed -- never sudo/askpass. Upstream gnustep-gui 0.32.0 contains no
sudo/askpass call site, so this patch ADDS a helper method
(-abzuAuthorizeAndRunAsRoot:) to NSWorkspace as Abzu-specific glue for
GWorkspace/AbzuShell callers; smoke-test on first overlay build.

Upstreaming: tracked per-patch in docs/ROADMAP.md.

---
---
diff --git a/Source/NSWorkspace.m b/Source/NSWorkspace.m
index 6bc7f71..efd8abb 100644
--- a/Source/NSWorkspace.m
+++ b/Source/NSWorkspace.m
@@ -1778,6 +1778,39 @@ inFileViewerRootedAtPath: (NSString*)rootFullpath
 		      autolaunch: NO];
 }
 
+/**
+ * Abzu overlay (security pillar): privileged shell helpers must be
+ * authorized through doas(1), which honours /etc/doas.conf shipped by
+ * build/derivations/rootfs.nix and fails closed -- never sudo/askpass.
+ * Callers in GWorkspace/AbzuShell pass the argv they want run as root.
+ */
+- (BOOL) abzuAuthorizeAndRunAsRoot: (NSArray *)argv
+{
+  NSMutableArray	*args;
+
+  if ([argv count] == 0 || [argv objectAtIndex: 0] == nil)
+    {
+      return NO;
+    }
+
+  args = [NSMutableArray arrayWithObject: @"-u"];
+  [args addObject: @"root"];
+  [args addObjectsFromArray: argv];
+
+  try
+    {
+      NSTask	*t = [NSTask launchedTaskWithLaunchPath: @"/usr/bin/doas"
+                            arguments: args];
+      [t waitUntilExit];
+      return ([t terminationStatus] == 0);
+    }
+  catch NSException *e
+    {
+      NSLog(@"Abzu doas launch failed: %@", [e name]);
+      return NO;
+    }
+}
+
